    "type": "question",
    "label": "27",
    "prompt": "Given $f(x)=(4x-1)(3x+2)^2$, find the equation of the tangent at the point where $x=-1$. Answer in general form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$34x-y+29=0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=4(3x+2)^2+6(4x-1)(3x+2)\\\\f'(x)&=2(3x+2)(18x+1)\\\\f'(-1)&=2(-1)(-17)=34\\\\f(-1)&=(-5)(-1)^2=-5\\end{align*}$$\nThe tangent passes through $(-1,-5)$ with gradient $34$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-(-5)&=34\\bigl(x-(-1)\\bigr)\\\\y+5&=34x+34\\\\34x-y+29&=0\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
